    "notes": [
      "The core regulator: VREG_VIN from 3.3 V, VREG_VOUT straight to both DVDD pins, 1 uF at its input and output.",
      "Keep the flash next to the QSPI pins with short traces; QSPI_SS pulled low at reset (BOOTSEL) starts the USB mass-storage bootloader."
    ],
    "page": "Hardware design with RP2040 (minimal design example); datasheet 2.9 Power supplies, 2.16 Crystal oscillator"
  },
  "notes": [
    "The exposed pad (57) is the chip's only ground: solder it, with several vias to the ground plane.",
    "The ePad is smaller than common QFN-56 footprints: use the datasheet's 3.2 mm pad, it leaves room to route between it and the pins.",
    "Program memory is external: a QSPI NOR flash (W25Q-series, up to 16 MB) is required.",
    "The USB bootloader needs a 12 MHz crystal or clock on XIN; USB_DP/USB_DM need 27 ohm series resistors, pull-ups are internal.",
    "TESTEN to GND. RUN low resets; SWCLK/SWDIO to a debug header.",
    "GPIO26-29 are the ADC inputs (ADC0-3), powered from ADC_AVDD; any GPIO can carry SIO, PIO0 or PIO1."
  ],
